\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec4 Notes from the AI Trenches \'97 What\'92s Working for the Enterprise\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\i\b0\fs24 \cf0 This write\uc0\u8209 up summarizes what I observed across recent talks, demos, and technical discussions, translated into practical guidance for business and engineering teams. The goal is clarity and actionability.
\f4\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf9 \strokec9 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec4 Executive Brief\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Agents are becoming production systems
\f4\b0 , not prototypes: identity, permissions, audit trails, and rollback are now table stakes.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Knowledge\uc0\u8209 RAG (graphs + vectors + search)
\f4\b0  is outperforming vectors alone for relationship, counting, and multi\uc0\u8209 step questions.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Relational predictions (RFM\uc0\u8209 style)
\f4\b0  allow agents to call churn/propensity/fraud scores directly from warehouse/graph context.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Multimodal ingestion
\f4\b0  (documents, tables, images, audio) in a single pipeline creates durable assets for search, graphs, BI, and compliance.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 Evaluation, safety, and performance
\f4\b0  are the difference between a demo and a deployable product.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf9 \strokec9 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec4 What Changed (and Why It Matters)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1) Agent Runtimes with Controls\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 Modern runtimes handle planning, tool use, memory, identity (OAuth/OIDC), observability, and kill\uc0\u8209 switches. The value is 
\f2\b operability
\f4\b0 : we can see what an agent planned, which tools it invoked, under which identity, and we can revoke access instantly if needed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Implication:
\f4\b0  Treat agents like microservices: owner, scoped permissions, rate limits, traces, and clear rollback procedures.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 2) Knowledge\uc0\u8209 RAG Instead of Vectors\u8209 Only\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 Graphs contribute explicit structure (entities, relationships, constraints). Paired with vector and full\uc0\u8209 text search, we get higher accuracy on multi\u8209 hop and aggregation questions. A lightweight 
\f2\b router
\f4\b0  determines whether to query vectors, graph (Text2Cypher), or both.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Implication:
\f4\b0  Store text as chunks (vector + full\uc0\u8209 text) and facts as triples (graph). Return answers with citations and, where relevant, the graph path used.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 3) Predictions on Relational Data (RFM\uc0\u8209 Style)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 Relational foundation models provide zero/low\uc0\u8209 shot predictions over business data: churn, next\u8209 best\u8209 action, fraud risk. Agents can call these scores mid\u8209 flow and justify actions with retrieved evidence.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Implication:
\f4\b0  Reasoning (LLM) + prediction (RFM\uc0\u8209 style) is a strong, repeatable pattern for outcomes that matter to the business.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 4) Multimodal Pipelines\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 A unified ingestion path (decode \uc0\u8594  clean \u8594  OCR \u8594  extract entities/relations \u8594  embed) produces 
\f2\b one source of truth
\f4\b0  used by search, graphs, analytics, and audit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Implication:
\f4\b0  Build once, reuse broadly; maintain lineage and hashes to preserve trust and reproducibility.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 5) Evaluation, Safety, and Performance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 Internal leaderboards (golden tasks), pre/post guardrails (PII/safety), and serving optimizations (speculative decoding, KV caching) are now standard practice.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Implication:
\f4\b0  We can scale only what we can measure, govern, and afford.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
