\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec4 FAQs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Do we need a whole new stack?
\f4\b0 \uc0\u8232 No. Add a graph database alongside your vector index, build the router, and wrap existing services as tools with scoped identities.\

\f2\b Is this only for developers?
\f4\b0 \uc0\u8232 No. Product and operations get grounded answers with sources; sales and care get clearer next\u8209 best actions; compliance gets better logs.\

\f2\b How difficult is the relational prediction piece?
\f4\b0 \uc0\u8232 Harder than a quick script, easier than six bespoke models. Start with a single prediction (e.g., churn). If ROI is clear, extend to NBA or fraud.\

\f2\b Are we locked to any single vendor?
\f4\b0 \uc0\u8232 Design the interfaces first (router, tools, registry). Vendors can be swapped behind these contracts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf9 \strokec9 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec4 Closing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs24 \cf0 The consistent pattern across sessions was not a new model; it was 
\f2\b operational maturity
\f4\b0 : agents that can be observed, governed, and rolled back. Combined with Knowledge\uc0\u8209 RAG and accessible predictions, that maturity turns impressive demos into dependable products. This is where we should invest.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

